.nh
.TH "TUSK" "1" "Jul 2026" "Tusk" "Tusk Manual"

.SH NAME
tusk-edge-list - List edges, optionally filtered by source, target, or kind


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtusk edge list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List edges in the index.

.PP
Filter with any combination of --from, --to, and --type. Output is a
tab-aligned table of source, type, target, attributed source-path. Use
--format compact|json (or --json) to opt into structured output; the
default mirrors prior CLI behavior (tab-aligned table for TTY).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--format\fP=""
	output format: compact|json (default: legacy table)

.PP
\fB--from\fP=""
	filter to edges originating from this source id

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	emit structured JSON (sugar for --format json)

.PP
\fB--to\fP=""
	filter to edges targeting this id

.PP
\fB--type\fP=""
	filter by edge type


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	emit debug-level logs to stderr


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # All edges that touch a node (either direction)
  tusk edge list --from tickets/T-001
  tusk edge list --to   tickets/T-001

  # Every "blocks" edge in the workspace
  tusk edge list --type blocks

  # JSON for piping into jq
  tusk edge list --from tickets/T-001 --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtusk-edge(1)\fP
